course: dictionary
lesson: 14269
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, read the words around it. «The ninja crept along the wall without a sound.» Crept, wall and without a sound are the clues, so a ninja here is a secret fighter or spy.
explain: The same word can also praise someone. «Ella is a maths ninja; she solved every puzzle.» The clue is solved every puzzle, so maths ninja means someone who is very skilled at maths. Nobody is fighting.
explain: Ask yourself: is this about sneaking and fighting, or about being very good at something? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A ninja is a secret fighter or spy from old Japan.
fact: Real ninjas were spies and scouts in Japan in the 1400s to 1600s, trained in fighting, sneaking and disguises.
fact: In stories, cartoons and games, ninjas often wear black and move silently.
fact: Informal use: «a spelling ninja» means a person who is very skilled at spelling.
fact: The plural of ninja is ninjas, and phrases like «ninja moves» and «ninja warrior» are common.
exercise: «The ninja crept along the wall without a sound.» In this sentence, what is a ninja? | A tall tree | A kind of wall | *A secret fighter or spy | A person who sings loudly
exercise: «Ella is a maths ninja; she solved every puzzle.» What does maths ninja mean? | *Someone very skilled at maths | A maths teacher from old Japan | A puzzle book | Someone who hates numbers
exercise: What is the plural of ninja? | ninjae | ninjies | ninja's | *ninjas
test: «The ninja hid in the shadows of the castle.» Which meaning fits? | A quiet kind of walk | *A secret fighter or spy | A black costume | A person who is very skilled at drawing
test: Which sentence uses ninja in the informal way? | «The ninja wore a black mask.» | *«Sam is a ninja at chess, he never loses.» | «The ninja hid behind the curtain.» | «The ninjas crept past the guards.»
exam: «Tom is a reading ninja.» Which meaning fits? | A quiet kind of walk | A trained fighter who wears black | A secret spy in old Japan | *A person who is very skilled at reading
